# Refrain (the original is in cut time; written here with quarter-note beats)
Charles-ton! Charles-ton! Made in Car-o-lin-a,
F4 r/ F4/ ~F4(2) F#4 r/ F#4/ ~F#4(2) G4 r/ G4/ ~G4/. F#4// G4 D5 r/ G4/ ~G4(2)
some dance, some prance, I'll say, there's noth-ing fin-er than the
G4 r/ D5/ ~D5(2) G4 r/ D5/ ~D5(2) G4 r/ Bb4/ ~Bb4(2) A4/ C5/ A4/ G4/ ~G4/ A4/ G4/. Gb4//
Charles-ton, Charles-ton. Lord, how you can shuf-fle!
F4 r/ F4/ ~F4(2) F#4 r/ F#4/ ~F#4(2) G4 r/ G4/ ~G4/. F#4// G4 D5 r/ D5/ ~D5(2)
Ev-'ry step you do leads to some-thing new,
r/ A4/ A4/ A4/ ~A4/ G4/ F4 r/ G4/ G4/ G4/ ~G4/ F4/ E4
man, I'm tell-ing you, it's a la-pa-zoo.
r/ A4/ A4/ A4/ ~A4/ G4/ F#4 r/ A4/ A4/ A4/ ~A4/ G4/ F4
Buck dance, wing dance will be a back num-ber,
F4 r/ F4/ ~F4(2) F#4 r/ F#4/ ~F#4(2) G4 r/ G4/ ~G4/. F#4// G4 D5 r/ G4/ ~G4/ r/
but the Charles-ton, the new Charles-ton, that dance is sure-ly a com-er.
G4/. G4// G4 r/ D5/ ~D5/. C#5// D5 G4 r/ D5/ ~D5(2) G4 r/ Bb4/ ~Bb4 Bb4 A4/ C5/ A4/ G4/ ~G4 F4
